            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with acute pain and swelling of her wrist].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A8623</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After hyperextension of both her wrists, a 39-year-old woman, who used coumarin derivatives for a known antiphospholipid syndrome, had acute pain and swelling of the left wrist. She had symptoms of an acute carpal tunnel syndrome. MRI revealed a hematoma compressing the median nerve in the carpal tunnel.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
